# SKU contract — single writer

Schema: `docs/references/customer-demo-sku-contract.md`.
Example: `datasets/sfdmu/customer-template/en-US/sku-contract.example.yaml`.

These three files are the shared interface between parallel customer demo builders.

| File | Written by | Read by |
|---|---|---|
| `sku-contract.yaml` | conductor, after the user confirms the vision | all builders |
| `customer-pricebook-entries.csv` | conductor, projected from the contract `skus` list | all builders, `customer_demo_recreate_pricebook_via_api`, `customer_demo_verify_catalog` |
| `org-context.json` | Org Discovery agent | all builders |

A domain builder that edits any of these breaks the other builders running in parallel. If a
builder needs a different value, it reports the mismatch and the conductor amends the
contract.

## Pricebook CSV columns

`SKU, UnitPrice, CurrencyIsoCode, PSMName, PSMSellingModelType, IsActive, CategoryCode,
ImageRequired, BillingRequired, BillingPolicyName, ProductTypeExpected, ExpectedPricingRules`

- `CategoryCode` must be populated — empty values make `customer_demo_verify_catalog` report
  a missing `ProductCategoryProduct` on every SKU.
- `ProductTypeExpected` is `Bundle` on bundle SKUs and empty on all others; verify then
  enforces Bundle vs blank rather than "any non-null type".
- `ExpectedPricingRules` drives the ABA count check.
- `PSMName` + `PSMSellingModelType` must exist in the org and match both
  `ProductSellingModelOption` in PCM and `RateCardEntry.ProductSellingModel` in rates.

## Changing the contract mid-run

Editing after builders have started invalidates their output. Stop the wave, edit the
contract, re-launch the affected builders, then re-run the Integrator.
